    "identity_1": "Sales forPay = priceWithDisc × (1 − commission_percent/100)   ⟹   gap = priceWithDisc × commission_percent/100",
    "identity_2": "Sales forPay = Finance ppvz_for_pay + acquiring_fee   (when both present on same SRID)",
    "implication": "From (2): acquiring_fee = Sales forPay − ppvz_for_pay. Acquiring is a split of Sales forPay into settlement for_pay + acquiring — it is not a term removed between priceWithDisc and Sales forPay.",
    "therefore": "acquiring ∉ (netSales − salesForPay). The entire gap is the commission-percent wedge on priceWithDisc."
  },
  "verdict": {
    "is_acquiring_economically_inside_netSales_minus_salesForPay": false,
    "proof": "On 100% of raw matched Продажа SRIDs, (priceWithDisc − salesForPay) = priceWithDisc × commission_percent/100 (residual 0). That identity fully accounts for the gap with no residual slot for acquiring. Separately, salesForPay = ppvz_for_pay + acquiring_fee on the majority of rows — acquiring is the difference between Sales forPay and Finance for_pay, i.e. it remains inside salesForPay, not inside the gap above it."
  }
